  Initial conditions of check-case 15: Appendix C.1.18, Table 42 (10,000
  ft MSL at 89.95 N 45 W, Earth-relative NED velocity [0, 563.643, 0]
  ft/s, heading 90 deg). The version 1 format is the one whose <trim>
  JSBSim runs before the first output: the longitudinal trim solves for
  zero udot, wdot and qdot by moving angle of attack (so pitch, keeping
  the flight path level), the throttle and the pitch trim, as the TM's
  trim varies pitch attitude, elevator and throttle. It sets the body
  rates to zero relative to the Earth.
  Written for jsbsim-rs from the parameters in NASA/TM-2015-218675,
  "Check-Cases for Verification of 6-Degree-of-Freedom Flight Vehicle
  Simulations", Volume II: Appendices.
-->
<initialize name="Atmos 15">
  <latitude unit="DEG" type="geodetic"> 89.95 </latitude>
  <longitude unit="DEG"> -45.0 </longitude>
  <altitudeMSL unit="FT"> 10000.0 </altitudeMSL>
  <phi unit="DEG"> 0.0 </phi>
  <theta unit="DEG"> 0.0 </theta>
  <psi unit="DEG"> 90.0 </psi>
  <vnorth unit="FT/SEC"> 0.0 </vnorth>
  <veast unit="FT/SEC"> 563.643 </veast>
  <vdown unit="FT/SEC"> 0.0 </vdown>
  <trim> longitudinal </trim>
</initialize>
